From 5d5b4669403b499373b48d72f65a5ad27ab8b8b7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 22:28:21 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] kanban: plugin start gate (kanban_start_gate hook)
 so a token throttle can hold card starts

The token throttle (hermes-mods throughput plugin) paces model calls, but the
dispatcher kept starting cards, so worker slots filled with runs that only
wait. Right before a claim the dispatcher now asks the kanban_start_gate
hook; {"hold": True, "reason": "<word>"} keeps the card ready and unclaimed
for that tick (respawn_guarded reason start_gate:<word>). Nothing is stored:
it is asked again every tick. No subscriber, a failing callback or any other
answer starts the card.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>
